2026-09-27T17:24:50.5471817Z     The ``pytest`` framework makes it easy to write small tests, yet
2026-09-27T17:24:50.5472043Z     scales to support complex functional testing for applications and libraries.
2026-09-27T17:24:50.5472127Z     
2026-09-27T17:24:50.5472231Z     An example of a simple test:
2026-09-27T17:24:50.5472306Z     
2026-09-27T17:24:50.5472407Z     .. code-block:: python
2026-09-27T17:24:50.5472488Z     
2026-09-27T17:24:50.5472590Z         # content of test_sample.py
2026-09-27T17:24:50.5472677Z         def inc(x):
2026-09-27T17:24:50.5472769Z             return x + 1
2026-09-27T17:24:50.5472851Z     
2026-09-27T17:24:50.5472927Z     
2026-09-27T17:24:50.5473027Z         def test_answer():
2026-09-27T17:24:50.5473122Z             assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-27T17:24:50.5473198Z     
2026-09-27T17:24:50.5473277Z     
2026-09-27T17:24:50.5473368Z     To execute it::
2026-09-27T17:24:50.5473446Z     
2026-09-27T17:24:50.5473533Z         $ pytest
